.TH VIEW 1
.SH NAME
view \- show meshes and pictures in a window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B view
[
.B \-c
|
.B \-b
]
.I scene
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I View
shows the meshes and pictures of a scene file,
.IR scene (5),
in a window.
A file of the scene is reloaded when it changes; a bad file is reported
and the old one kept.
.PP
With the mouse, a left drag turns the view, a middle or right drag
moves it, and the wheel zooms about the pointer.
A click picks a part (its name is printed, shown in the lower left,
and the part highlighted).
A shift and left drag on a part pulls its scene item out along the line
from the centre, never past home.
.PP
Keys:
.TP 8
Space
Fit all.
.TP
.B "i f b l r t u"
Iso, front, back, left, right, top, bottom.
.TP
.B h
Hide the part under the pointer.
.TP
.B o
Show only the part under the pointer.
.TP
.B s
Make the part under the pointer see-through, or solid again.
.TP
.B a
Show all, all solid, all home.
.TP
.B "+ \-"
Explode a step of 0.25 further, or back, stopping at home.
.TP
.B "^Z ^Y"
Undo, redo (of what is shown, see-through and moved; not the camera).
.TP
.B ?
Help, on or off.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
Commands are read from the standard input, one per line;
a pattern matches names, * for any run of characters:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hide|show|only|see|solid PATTERN
all, reset, home, undo, redo
key h|o|s X Y          the key with the pointer at pixel X Y
explode F              F from 0 (home) to 100
drag NAME D            NAME D mm out, not less than 0
view iso|front|back|left|right|top|bottom
fit, turn DX DY, zoom F, size W H
pick X Y               print the name there, or \-
list                   NAME TRIS shown|hidden solid|see at X Y Z
shot FILE.ppm
spin N                 N frames of a turn about z
help, quit
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B Reset
is the
.B a
key,
.B home
sets every offset to 0, and the position in a list line is the centre
of the part's box.
.TP
.B \-c
Check the scene, print
.I "name tris"
for each part, and quit.
.TP
.B \-b
Read the commands without a window;
.B shot
then draws on the processor.
.SH SEE ALSO
scene(5), tomesh(1)
